{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-12285" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x-4y=2 \\\\ -x+y=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-12285" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 1-(-4)\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-12285" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "55680662e343d8642019ae35fdd2c34e732df2e04e4b1f1a359268d0415ff90e"} {"question" "q-12285" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/j