ion" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 1-6\\cdot 8}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-32139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "55680662e343d8642019ae35fdd2c34e732df2e04e4b1f1a359268d0415ff90e"} {"question" "q-32139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-32139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 \\\\ -6 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{50}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{50}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-32139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-102802" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y=4 \\\\ 6=5x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-102802" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y=4 \\\\ 5x=6.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-102802" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "55680662e343d8642019ae35fdd2c34e732df2e04e4b1f1a359268d0415ff90e"} {"question" "q-102802" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-102802" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-102802" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-320805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=7 \\\\ 5x+2y=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-5$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $7$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-3$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-4$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-5$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $7$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-3$ |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-320805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-320805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "55680662e343d8642019ae35fdd2c34e732df2e04e4b1f1a359268d0415ff90e"} {"question" "q-320805" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-320805" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{18}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-320805" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-320805" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-320805" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-320805" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-320836" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+8=0 \\\\ x=7+3y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $-3$ | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-1$ | {{field-2}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $7$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-3$ | $0$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $7$ |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-320836" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+0y=-8 \\\\ x-3y=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-320836" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "55680662e343d8642019ae35fdd2c34e732df2e04e4b1f1a359268d0415ff90e"} {"question" "q-320836" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-320836" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{12}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "f48ef8f6e8ff36786dcc1262b35644b0cb2f3e97d25f1dda16dca5b9469c8210"} {"question" "q-320836" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacadem